<main id="main-content"><section class="section"><div class="container article-body" style="max-width:850px"><div class="notice notice-error" style="margin-bottom:24px"><strong>Draft notice for review.</strong> OCG should confirm this text matches its actual data-handling practices, retention periods and applicable requirements before the website is made public.</div><h2>Information collected</h2><p>The website may collect information you choose to provide in contact, partnership or feedback forms, such as your name, organisation, email address, phone number, message and optional proposal attachment.</p><h2>How information is used</h2><p>Submitted information is intended to be used to review and respond to your enquiry, assess a proposed collaboration, or understand feedback about OCG’s public information. The form fields should not be used to request passwords, payment card numbers or other highly sensitive information.</p><h2>Attachments and storage</h2><p>Optional partnership attachments are saved in a protected server directory and are not intended to be available through a public web link. The hosting administrator should restrict access to submitted files, review them using appropriate security practices and remove them when no longer needed under OCG’s approved retention process.</p><h2>Email and hosting</h2><p>Form submissions are sent through the website host’s configured email service to the contact address shown on this website. The hosting provider may process technical information required to operate the website. OCG should update this section if it introduces analytics, third-party form services, mailing lists or other integrations.</p><h2>Retention and contact</h2><p>OCG should retain submissions only as long as needed for the stated purpose and the organisation’s approved policies. For questions about a submission, contact <a class="text-link" href="mailto:<?= e(SITE_EMAIL) ?>"><?= e(SITE_EMAIL) ?> <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.</p><h2>Before production</h2><p>Confirm the responsible data controller, the final retention schedule, approved access roles, backup procedures, and any applicable notice or consent requirements. Remove this draft warning only after OCG approves the notice.</p></div></section></main>
